<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.pool.checks ~ check ~ a pool holds its own identity alone

`lares surface check` reads the repo at the working directory (or the `--face N` pool) and refuses an index file or another face's root in the pool, a repo at projections/ or config/, and an author or signing key another face's pool carries. A realm tree reads under the realm check; `--realm <realm pet name>` checks every tree the realm's wikis rest in. A breach exits 1 and names each, with its pool.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ here · realm

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`here` params=`~ check the repo at the working directory`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`realm` params=`realm/notes ~ check every pool of the realm`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ face · realm

<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/face`>>

